Possible spoilers (pretty minor)


I'll admit that subject line probably looks pretty random and it is, but this
is just sort of an eclectic bunch of thoughts on my first run through of 3.1.

Holy water - I know this is a FAQ, but I never paid attention. How do you 
turn normal water into holy water. I thought in 3.0 simply putting it on a
lawful altar did the trick, but not so here.

Heart of Ahriman - What does it do? I know it's beneficial and it does give the
cool "Power surges through you" message whenever you pick it up, but I'm 
unable to apply it, wear it, or do much else except put it in my backpack. 
Does simply carrying it help you and, if so, what does it do? 

Hell - What's the story with lawful characters and praying in hell? I'm
running a lawful barbarian about the enter Hell and seem to remember something
from the 3.0 discussions on the topic (never affected me since the few times
I got that far in 3.0 I was a chaotic valkyrie).

Dropped stuff in water - How do you get it out w/o an amulet of magical 
breathing? Thanks to the wonders of a type-ahead buffer, I managed to   
accidentally stray into the water on the medusa level and drop, among other
things, Excalibur. I've got rings of both polymorph and polymorph control, but
can't think of anything offhand that will do the trick. Water nymph let me
swim, but not dive to the bottom, and water elementals don't have hands. Is
there any form that _would_ be able to retrieve things from the water?

Medusa - I'd blinded myself to see if this was indeed her level once I started
finding the statues (I had ESP). Suddenly, she disappeared. I assumed maybe
she climbed the stairs or something and turned into a vampire lord to go see.
When I got there, all I found was a statue of Medusa. How did she stone herself?

Wishs - My first one took me by surprise. After two #sits on a throne both
gave me genocide (liches and gremlins), the next gave me a wish. Quite a 
change from the ones I ran into in 3.0 which always seemed to make me lose me
gold or do nothing. That one went for GDSM since I needed the resistane and
better armor. I knew I had a magic lamp in my inventory, but applying it
only lit up the area. Needless to say, I was happy when, while reading through
the command help file, I noticed #rub - wish #2 went for a blessed bag of
holding since I already had reflection, Excalibur (before the runin with the
water), and most everything I could think of. Since I'm nearly at the castle,
what would you recommend next for wishing?

Polymorphing - I remember a week or so ago, some people posted lists of 
fun/interesting/powerful things to polymorph into. Now that I've finally got
both polymorph and control, I'd like to give it a shot. Currently, I've     
basically stuck with dragon, vampire lord, and xorn, depending on the situation
but if someone had that list and could Email me, I'd appreciate it.

Well, that's about it. I think this character has a good shot at winning, 
though I'd really like to get Excalibur back from its current watery grave.

Thanks for any answers or observations on the questions I raised.
